<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Major still doubts EMU will start on time.</title>
<headline>Major still doubts EMU will start on time.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister John Major said he still doubted the European Union would launch a single currency on time in January 1999, despite accords on Friday on budget discipline and the presentation of the future banknotes.</p>
<p>Major acknowledged that EU countries were making &quot;herculean efforts&quot; to meet the criteria for monetary union and there would be a determined effort to start on time.</p>
<p>Reaffirming Britain's wait-and-see attitude to joining the euro, he told a news conference: &quot;It is by no means certain that they will reach January 1, 1999...I am very doubtful about that.&quot;</p>
</text>
